A||||4||alpha||Where to get metal brake lines?||||1||
Z||000000||alpha||10-31-2000||02:33 PM||||Okay, here is the story. The metal brake line which feeds the rear brakes broke just before the distribution block next to the right rear wheel.<P>I can't seem to find ANY sources for the larger metric lines and fittings. I have found a place which carries the smaller lines, but not the bigger stuff.<P>I know 1/4" will not work (I learned that the hard way) and I can't flare the metric line with the 1/4" part of my flaring tool.<P>Is there anyone who sells this larger (6mm I think) metric line in straight sections? Or is there anyone who sells an adapter to go from SAE flare to metric flare? I can't seem to find anyone.<P>I am sure at least a few people have had this problem.<P>Any help, suggestions or comments would be greatly appreciated.<P>--Douglas Knight||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-31-2000||04:24 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.napaonline.com" TARGET=_blank>www.napaonline.com</A>   goodluck! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||alpha||10-31-2000||05:12 PM||||Unfortunally I have tried NAPA (and reviewed <A HREF="http://www.napaonline.com)" TARGET=_blank>www.napaonline.com)</A>  and have not found anything. In the store all they seemed to have was SAE, not that the counter person was a lot of help.<P>--Douglas Knight||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||11-01-2000||09:02 AM||||Autozone has metric brake lines in different lengths, hopefully one long enough.  Only catch is you'll need a brake line bender because the lines are straight.<P>Take the old line and measure the length from bend to bend and see if they have one long enough first.  Then use the old line as a pattern to bend a new line.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||alpha||11-01-2000||10:57 AM||||Someone else suggested Autozone. I am going to call them today to find out if they have the 6mm stuff which no one seems to have.<P>I have a bender and am prepared to bend, I just can't find the right thing to bend.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for the input.<P>--Douglas Knight||||reg||1
